-- An illustrative rule, not a statute: a filing is required of every kind of
-- body except the residual one, unless the body is licensed, dormant or
-- publicly funded.
--
-- The exception is one rung of the ladder and three conditions.
-- The twelve kinds make the first eight inputs that realise "the exception
-- applies" all share one combination of the three, which is what a gate that
-- cares only about the rung can be satisfied by.
DECLARE Category IS ONE OF
  Individual, Partnership, Company, Trust, Charity, Cooperative,
  Estate, Club, Society, Fund, Syndicate, Other

@export default Whether a filing is required of a body
GIVEN category IS A Category
      `holds a licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is dormant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is publicly funded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `filing is required` IF
      NOT (category EQUALS Other)
  UNLESS `holds a licence`
      OR `is dormant`
      OR `is publicly funded`
